From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: a larger BO when a streamed texture goes linear

After a few complete overwrites a u-interleaved texture is switched to
linear in place, in the same BO, with only an assert that the linear
layout fits. Linear rows are aligned to 64 bytes and tiled ones to 16,
so at some widths it does not: an R8 plane of a 1480x1080 video needs
1536 x 1080 bytes linear (0x195000) against 1488 x 1088 tiled (0x18c000
in pages). The copy then ran off the mapping: mpv segfaulted about eight
frames into the video, with software decoding too, or corrupted whatever
followed when the BO cache had handed out a larger BO. Allocate a BO
that fits, stay tiled when that fails, and re-emit the descriptors,
whose layout just changed.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -1915,16 +1915,40 @@
                panfrost_resource_setup(screen, prsrc, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR,
                                        prsrc->image.layout.format);
 
-               /* converting the resource from tiled to linear and back
-                * shouldn't increase memory usage...
-                */
-               assert(prsrc->image.layout.data_size <= panfrost_bo_size(bo));
+               /* Linear rows are aligned to 64 bytes, so at some widths the
+                * linear layout needs more than the tiled one (R8 1480x1080:
+                * 1536 x 1080 bytes against 1488 x 1088, 0x195000 and
+                * 0x18c000 in pages): it takes a larger BO then. */
+               if (prsrc->image.layout.data_size > panfrost_bo_size(bo)) {
+                  struct panfrost_bo *newbo = panfrost_bo_create(
+                     dev, prsrc->image.layout.data_size,
+                     bo->flags & ~PAN_BO_DELAY_MMAP, bo->label);
 
-               util_copy_rect(
-                  bo->ptr.cpu + prsrc->image.layout.slices[0].offset,
-                  prsrc->base.format, prsrc->image.layout.slices[0].row_stride,
-                  0, 0, transfer->box.width, transfer->box.height, trans->map,
-                  transfer->stride, 0, 0);
+                  if (newbo) {
+                     panfrost_bo_unreference(bo);
+                     bo = prsrc->bo = newbo;
+                     prsrc->image.data.base = newbo->ptr.gpu;
+                  } else {
+                     panfrost_resource_setup(
+                        screen, prsrc,
+                        DRM_FORMAT_MOD_ARM_16X16_BLOCK_U_INTERLEAVED,
+                        prsrc->image.layout.format);
+                     panfrost_store_tiled_images(trans, prsrc);
+                     bo = NULL;
+                  }
+               }
+
+               if (bo) {
+                  /* The layout changed: new descriptors. */
+                  panfrost_dirty_state_all(ctx);
+
+                  util_copy_rect(
+                     bo->ptr.cpu + prsrc->image.layout.slices[0].offset,
+                     prsrc->base.format,
+                     prsrc->image.layout.slices[0].row_stride, 0, 0,
+                     transfer->box.width, transfer->box.height, trans->map,
+                     transfer->stride, 0, 0);
+               }
             } else {
                panfrost_store_tiled_images(trans, prsrc);
             }
